# CODEOWNERS — the recursion break for the ship gate.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# `.github/workflows/preship-verify.yml` re-runs the audit server-side, where the coding
# agent has no write access at merge time and no access to the API keys. But for a
# `pull_request` event GitHub runs the workflow file FROM THE PR BRANCH — so an agent
# could weaken or delete the check in the same PR that needs it.
#
# Two things close that, and neither is something the agent can grant itself:
#   1. Branch protection requires a status check BY NAME ("preship"). Delete or rename
#      the job and the required check never reports, so the PR can never merge —
#      weakening the file permanently BLOCKS the merge rather than unblocking it.
#   2. This file. Any change under .github/ or .claude/preship/ requires Rafael's
#      explicit review before it can merge, enforced by
#      "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rule.
#
# LIVE STATE 2026-07-22 (from the branch-protection API, not assumed):
#   enforce_admins .................... TRUE   ✓ (admins cannot bypass)
#   allow_force_pushes ................ FALSE  ✓
#   required_pull_request_reviews ..... present (count 0 — solo config)
#   require_code_owner_reviews ........ FALSE  ✗  <-- MUST be enabled for this file
#                                                    to have any teeth.
#   required_status_checks.contexts ... []     ✗  <-- "preship" not yet required;
#                                                    add it after the workflow's first run.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS only has teeth when "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled on
# the protected branch. Until that tick is on, this file is advisory only. Operator
# action required — see the two settings in .github/ setup notes.

